        <headline>Small Craft Advisory issued September 24 at 12:47PM AKDT until September 25 at 6:00PM AKDT by NWS Juneau AK</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...For the first Small Craft Advisory, seas 6 to 9 ft. For
the second Small Craft Advisory, southeast winds 20 to 25 kt
and seas 6 to 9 ft expected.

* WHERE...Icy Cape to Cape Suckling from 15 to 80 NM.

* WHEN...For the first Small Craft Advisory, until 7 PM AKDT
this evening. For the second Small Craft Advisory, from 7 AM
to 6 PM AKDT Friday.

* IMPACTS...Conditions will be hazardous to small craft.
</description>
        <instruction>Inexperienced mariners, especially those operating smaller
vessels, should avoid navigating in hazardous conditions.</instruction>
